<%#
  A PROJECT'S OWN LEFT COLUMN (the Shop manual, slice 5; its spec §7: "on a project, its contents,
  then the projects"), supplied by projects/show through `content_for :column` in place of the
  section's default (layouts/column/_projects).

  CONTENTS: Overview — the head, `#overview`, and the one lit row on this page
  (ShellHelper#projects_current answers `[:project_overview, id]` here) — then every section the page
  drew, in the page's order, each with the number its head carries and the count its head's note
  gave. Both come from the render that just happened: @page_sections is what the slots numbered
  (ProjectsHelper#section_number!) and @section_counts what the heads recorded
  (ProjectsHelper#section_note), so the column issues no query and cannot disagree with the page. A
  zero is not shown: an empty panel's head shows none either. Each row links to the panel's own
  element (ProjectsHelper#section_anchor), which tabs_controller.js follows into a closed tab; below
  960px, where this column is a sheet, following one closes the sheet over the page it points into.

  PROJECTS: the eight the section's default lists (ShellHelper#sidebar_projects, ONE query, the
  default's own), then All projects and New project. This project's own row is marked as this one
  (`column-row--this`) and never lit: the lit row is Overview, and a column lights at most one
  (design-system.md rule 8).
%>
<div class="column-group project-contents">
  <h2 class="column-head">Contents</h2>
  <%= link_to "#overview", class: "column-row column-row--section", "aria-current": row_aria([ :project_overview, @project.id ]),
              data: { action: "click->shell#closeColumn" } do %>
    <span class="column-row-num" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="column-row-name">Overview</span>
  <% end %>
  <%# TIDY UP (the Shop manual's §9), unnumbered like Overview because it is not one of the page's
      sections, with the plate's own count: @tidy is what the page drew, so this asks nothing. %>
  <% if @tidy&.any? %>
    <%= link_to "#tidy-up", class: "column-row column-row--section", data: { action: "click->shell#closeColumn" } do %>
      <span class="column-row-num" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="column-row-name">Tidy up</span>
      <span class="column-row-note"><%= @tidy.count %></span>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <% Array(@page_sections).each_with_index do |key, i| %>
    <% count = @section_counts&.[](key) %>
    <%= link_to "##{section_anchor(key)}", class: "column-row column-row--section", data: { action: "click->shell#closeColumn" } do %>
      <span class="column-row-num"><%= i + 1 %></span>
      <span class="column-row-name"><%= section_label(key) %></span>
      <% if count.to_i.positive? %><span class="column-row-note"><%= count %></span><% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
<div class="column-group">
  <h2 class="column-head">Projects</h2>
  <% sidebar_projects.each do |project| %>
    <%= column_row project.name, project_path(project), key: [ :project, project.id ],
                   class: ("column-row--this" if project.id == @project.id) %>
  <% end %>
  <%= column_row "All projects", projects_path, key: [ :all_projects ] %>
  <%= column_row "New project", new_project_path, key: [ :new_project ] %>
</div>
